# What the boundary lint (boundary.mjs) lets through today: one line per file and
# rule, `<path> <rule> <count>`, sorted, with an optional ` # why`. The count is
# exact, so this list only shrinks: a slice lowers or deletes the lines of the
# files it changes (`node scripts/loops/boundary.mjs --write` rewrites the counts).
.github/workflows/ci.yml project-to-core 1 # ci.yml's tooling jobs run the core's tests and lints: the removal commit drops them at the move
package.json project-to-core 4 # the package scripts run the core (its two commands, the tooling tests): the risa install replaces them at the move
risa.json project-to-core 1 # hooks.lease is the core's lease.sh hold, which the app's browser lease helper runs: its path changes at the move
scripts/ci/blame.test.mjs app-path 1 # a core test's throwaway repo runs on Caretook's config (config-fixture.mjs), so its made-up files sit in Caretook's folders: they take the sample project's at the move
scripts/ci/ci.test.mjs app-path 4 # a core test's throwaway repo runs on Caretook's config (config-fixture.mjs), so its made-up files sit in Caretook's folders: they take the sample project's at the move
scripts/ci/test-job.mjs project-to-core 2 # CI's test step feeds the core's time gate (one module judges every measure) with the gates' data: the tool's package at the move
scripts/ci/tiers.json project-to-core 1 # the tier data's tooling file group (the browser harness test): residual until the move
scripts/ci/tiers.test.mjs project-to-core 1 # compares the core's tier reader with this one until the move; the removal commit drops that half
scripts/ci/verdict.test.mjs project-to-core 2 # ties the core's verdict fixtures and reader version to the writer, buildVerdict: the core keeps the fixtures at the move, this half goes with the writer
scripts/deploy/workflows.test.mjs project-to-core 3 # the deploy workflow test pins ci.yml's tooling jobs, which run the core: until the move
scripts/loops/boundary.mjs core-to-project 2 # the manifest's folders (ROOTS) name the hooks folder and scripts/project: goes with the manifest at the move
scripts/loops/boundary.test.mjs core-to-project 1 # checks the manifest's folders (ROOTS), scripts/project among them: goes with the manifest at the move
scripts/loops/check-gate.test.mjs app-path 7 # a core test's throwaway repo runs on Caretook's config (config-fixture.mjs), so its made-up files sit in Caretook's folders: they take the sample project's at the move
scripts/loops/codex-review.fixtures/out-of-credits.json app-path 2 # a recorded Codex review of a Caretook PR: the fixture is rerecorded on the sample project at the move
